# Situation, not chance, not instruction

The DANA map paints a **level / situation**. The user decides what to do.

- Do not show a probability or “X% chance of flood” unless it comes from ECMWF IFS ENS member spread (51 members at 0.25°, Open-Meteo Ensemble API) **and** that spread is calibrated on labelled events. Open-Meteo `precipitation_probability` is a rain-bundle input, not a UI percentage.
- Do not add directive copy (“go upstairs”, “evacuate”, “stay off the rambla”, “leave now”). Level hints describe weather, not behaviour.
- Official warnings stay AEMET / 112 links. This desk is not a warning service.
- AROME (`/v1/meteofrance`, `models=arome_france` explicit) is a parallel backtest source. Less wrong on one Magre cell can still be 3× short of ~700 mm. Do not fold it into live scoring. `corridorBelt` is a table label: do not call inland-AROME a rule before a majority across `INLAND_AROME_RULE_MIN_CELLS` (6) independent **inland-orographic** labelled cells. Mallorca is island. Málaga / Almería / Gibraltar are south and always out of AROME domain — they will never yield AROME comparison rows, so inland-6 stays on labelled cells in the Valencia / Murcia / Catalonia corridors.
- Murcia Sep 2023 AROME all-null is an Open-Meteo **archive gap**, not a model miss and not the inland/coast tally.
- An AROME-only false alarm is hangover or leftover-rain (or unassigned) — never a new “AROME FA” bucket.
- SAIH gauges come later, to **calibrate ECMWF ENS members**, not to let AROME into the live score. Do not stack both unproven changes at once.
